-- title:
--   Literal discounted original source Taylor jump expectation equals the exact stopped nonlinear Lévy generator drift
-- statement:
--   For the original stopped controlled prepayment surplus, negative-extended C² value w, interior localization [u+δ,v], true ruin clock, q-discount finite physical horizon, and genuine source marks, the literal original-source Taylor jump sum is P-integrable and its expectation is exactly the predictable physical-clock integral of the spectrally negative Lévy generatorIntegrand. Uses the Proved Chat02 physical-clock L1 compensation and Proved Chat04 product generator drift, with the actual source future rectangle compensator hFuture explicitly assumed; makes no false claim that an arbitrary clock is source intensity or that the remaining Chat01 rectangle theorem is proved.
-- source:
--   Original mission 1300fbe7-ca8c-49f9-a4de-4cb35ebd2f43, Chat04 source-specific exact drift handoff; strictly combines canonical Proved 9d6ab3d0 and 10f8419c with discounted weight ed5ee649. Explicit hFuture remains Chat01-dependent.

